3.How would you design a Dart class to represent this order? Explain the role of the constructor, describe how you would create multiple order objects in your program, and explain how Dart's strong typing helps
avoid data errors at compile time.

A class groups related data into one object. The constructor initializes each order's fields, and multiple objects can represent different orders.

class FoodOrder {
  int orderId;
  String customerName;
  List<String> items;
  double totalAmount;

  FoodOrder({
    required this.orderId,
    required this.customerName,
    required this.items,
    required this.totalAmount,
  });
}

void main() {
  FoodOrder order1 = FoodOrder(
    orderId: 101,
    customerName: 'Rahul',
    items: ['Pizza', 'Burger'],
    totalAmount: 450.0,
  );

  FoodOrder order2 = FoodOrder(
    orderId: 102,
    customerName: 'Priya',
    items: ['Sandwich', 'Juice'],
    totalAmount: 250.0,
  );

  print(order1.customerName);
  print(order2.items);
}
